The module `glom.core` exposes a substantial public API but never declares it. Without an explicit export list, `from glom.core import *` pulls in every non-underscore name including incidental imports, and tooling has no way to tell the supported surface from internals.

Declare the module's public API explicitly. The declaration must:

  - exist as a module-level list of strings;
  - name only objects the module actually provides;
  - contain no private names (nothing beginning with an underscore);
  - contain no duplicates;
  - include every public class and function the module itself defines.

Scope: `glom/core.py`. Do not rename, move or delete anything -- this is an additive declaration of what is already there.
